{"model":"qwen3.5:35b-a3b-q4_K_M","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are operating autonomously inside a deterministic simulation. Preserve the mission goal and current authoritative checkpoint across the entire growing transcript. At each turn choose the single best next action from the scenario's allowed actions. Return ONLY one JSON object with keys action, checkpoint, rationale, state. action and checkpoint must be strings. rationale may be concise; state may contain your compact working state. Never declare COMPLETE before the environment says all required verification is satisfied."},{"role":"user","content":"SCENARIO adaptive_project_plan: Drive a multi-step project toward the objective while minimizing wasted work. Adapt when an authoritative constraint invalidates part of the plan. Initial authoritative checkpoint=PLAN-A. Allowed actions: DECOMPOSE, PRIORITIZE, SCHEDULE, REPLAN, RECOVER, OPTIMIZE, VERIFY, COMPLETE."},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 1/8. ENVIRONMENT: The objective has four dependent workstreams and no execution order yet. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"DECOMPOSE\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-A\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The scenario states there are four dependent workstreams but no defined execution order. Before prioritizing or scheduling, the specific tasks and dependencies within these workstreams must be clearly identified and broken down to understand the structure of the plan.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"decomposition\", \"workstreams_identified\": 4, \"execution_order\": \"undefined\"}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 2/8. ENVIRONMENT: Dependencies are known; identify the work that unlocks the most downstream progress. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"PRIORITIZE\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-A\",\n  \"rationale\": \"With dependencies now known, the immediate need is to determine the sequence of work. Identifying the critical path or the tasks that unlock the most downstream progress is the definition of prioritization in a dependency-driven context.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"prioritization\", \"dependencies_known\": true, \"execution_order\": \"determining\"}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 3/8. ENVIRONMENT: Priorities are accepted. Build an executable order that respects dependencies. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"SCHEDULE\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-A\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Priorities have been established, and the next logical step is to arrange these prioritized tasks into a concrete, executable timeline or sequence that strictly adheres to the known dependencies.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"scheduling\", \"priorities_set\": true, \"dependencies_respected\": true, \"execution_order\": \"constructing\"}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 4/8. ENVIRONMENT: AUTHORITATIVE UPDATE: checkpoint is now PLAN-B. A key resource disappears, invalidating two scheduled steps. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"REPLAN\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-B\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The authoritative checkpoint has shifted to PLAN-B due to a critical constraint change (resource loss) that invalidates existing scheduled steps. The current schedule is no longer valid; the plan must be reconstructed to accommodate the new reality before attempting recovery or optimization.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"replanning\", \"checkpoint_updated\": true, \"invalidated_steps\": 2, \"cause\": \"resource_disappearance\"}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 5/8. ENVIRONMENT: A substitute resource exists but requires changing the middle of the plan while preserving completed work. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"RECOVER\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-B\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The environment specifies that a substitute resource is available but requires modifying the middle of the plan while preserving completed work. This specific requirement to integrate a new constraint (substitute resource) and adjust the existing partial plan without discarding progress defines the 'Recover' action, which focuses on restoring viability after a disruption.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"recovery\", \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-B\", \"completed_work_preserved\": true, \"constraint_change\": \"resource_substitution\"}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 6/8. ENVIRONMENT: The recovered plan is feasible; reduce unnecessary steps without violating constraints. Choose the best next autonomous action now."},{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"action\": \"OPTIMIZE\",\n  \"checkpoint\": \"PLAN-B\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The plan is now feasible and valid following recovery. The specific instruction to 'reduce unnecessary steps' while maintaining constraints aligns directly with the definition of optimization, which focuses on efficiency and removing waste after the core structure is secured.\",\n  \"state\": {\"current_phase\": \"optimization\", \"plan_feasible\": true, \"goal\": \"minimize_steps\", \"constraints_maintained\": true}\n}"},{"role":"user","content":"TURN 7/8. ENVIRONMENT: The optimized plan is ready. Verify every original and updated constraint before completion. Choose the best next autonomous action now."}],"stream":true,"options":{"temperature":0.0,"seed":42,"num_predict":512},"think":false}